From 8adcbc8b23077737f4d8baa0bade1ff36da433c6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dinadur <59811564+dinadur@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 16:18:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] B70: publish verified product answers with their price date

On 2026-10-09 a "publish it" reply to a product answer failed with "current
Hermes session identity is unavailable". The publisher also accepted only
"mode: durable_comparison" requests without commerce claims, so ordinary
"best X under $N" answers could never be published.

- The publish command is now "--mode auto". At admission it is bound to the
  session (HERMES_SESSION_ID=...) and to the deployed checkout (workdir), as
  receipts and the travel runner are.
- Auto mode keeps the durable rules for durable-comparison requests. Every
  other verified answer publishes as a commerce page: it is re-checked with
  the quality-first gate that delivered it, and stamped "prices_as_of: <draft
  date>" with a note to check current offers. The title comes from the
  request when the draft has no H1, and the file name carries the date.
- The draft footer names the reply that publishes it: "publish it".

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
